  "solution": {
    "brief": "Wasp field-driven aggregation: scalar fields influence part placement and selection, biasing growth toward attractors or density gradients",
    "principle": "\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Tutorial 16 (wasp_16) extends field-driven aggregation concepts further into advanced territory, introducing isoline-based techniques and 3d-populate strategies. Isolines (contour lines of scalar fields) appear as a new tool in the field-driven workflow, suggesting that scalar field outputs can be used to generate isoline geometry that guides or constrains aggregation. The 3d-populate tag indicates volumetric population/distribution techniques that complement field-driven placement.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Tutorial 17 (wasp_17) continues the field-driven series beyond tutorial 16, further advancing scalar-field biased-growth and parametric-growth techniques for discrete aggregation. The progression from wasp_04 through wasp_16 to wasp_17 shows an evolving field-driven workflow where isolines, 3d-populate, and custom-preview become increasingly integrated tools for controlling aggregation behavior.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Tutorial 19 (wasp_19) continues the field-driven series through at least tutorial 19, introducing voxel-based techniques as a further evolution of the scalar-field-driven aggregation workflow. The progression from wasp_04 through wasp_16, wasp_17, wasp_18, to wasp_19 shows an increasingly complex field-driven workflow where voxel geometry and parametric-assembly strategies become integrated tools.\n\nRelated insight: Related insight: Tutorial 20 (wasp_20) continues the field-driven series through at least tutorial 20, introducing mesh-based and constraint-based techniques as further evolution of the scalar-field-driven aggregation workflow. The progression from wasp_04 through wasp_16, wasp_17, wasp_18, wasp_19, to wasp_20 shows an increasingly complex field-driven workflow where mesh geometry and constraint-based assembly become integrated tools.",
